  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given the three numbers \\(x,\\) \\(y=x^x,\\) \\(z=x^{(x^x)},\\) with \\(0.9\\lt x\\lt1.0.\\) Arranged in order of increasing magnitude, they are:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x,\\) \\(z,\\) \\(y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) \\(z\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(y,\\) \\(x,\\) \\(z\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(y,\\) \\(z,\\) \\(x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(z,\\) \\(x,\\) \\(y\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p29.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(0\\lt x\\lt1\\) and \\(x\\lt1,\\) raising \\(x\\) to the exponent \\(x\\) gives \\(x\\lt y=x^x\\lt1.\\) For a base between \\(0\\) and \\(1,\\) a larger exponent gives a smaller value. Because \\(x\\lt y\\lt1,\\) we have \\(x=x^1\\lt x^y=z\\lt x^x=y.\\) Thus \\(x\\lt z\\lt y.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "For \\(0\\lt x\\lt1,\\) compare powers by comparing their positive exponents",
        "First show \\(x\\lt x^x\\lt1\\), then compare \\(x^{x^x}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
